{
 "meta": {
  "name": "golden_property_documents",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "231 (stage D, D-e2): invented documents of businesses asking for property insurance (jav/evals/property_documents.py): quote request forms, a property schedule per site and claims history statements, in sets. Each document is kept as what a correct reading of it gives (its type pack's values; a null value is not printed); its printed page is made from them in the layout it names (standard, two_pages). Each set names the facts its documents hold through the fact readings (configs/fact_readings_property.json): the units, the values not read and the facts two documents disagree on. The first five sets hold the invented product set's reference cases (configs/golden_products.json, the case named), so their documents are read into the very facts the rules were measured on; the other three are a policyholder with two sites, a claims statement with another tax number and a schedule with words no code table knows. The printed text is document vocabulary (Hungarian); every name, address and number is invented, the tax numbers are on the data guard's list of invented values.",
  "changelog": [
   {
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "date": "2026-10-26",
    "note": "231 (D-e2): the first version: eight sets, 23 documents."
   }
  ]
 },
